/-!
# Observer licences for search and collection consumers

`Presentations` separates answer bags from declared enumerations. `Table`
provides one admission entry point and its semantic law catalogue; weighted
counting has a separate preferred-error readout. `PortfolioBridge` connects
actual bounded batches to finite bag selection and imports the unbounded
witness/continuation results from `PortfolioReach`.

The HE modules give a success-priority boundary, distinct DFS and deepening
controls, arbitrary-schedule publication safety and a constructive budgeted
publication theorem. Errors are value replies, not host raises.

Native classifiers must establish purity, read stability, complete inner
aggregates, the observer boundary and any commuting-fold evidence. Native
budget accounting, ownership and representation remain separate refinements.
-/
